<title>USA: New York $1.7 bln green bond approved by voters.</title>
<headline>New York $1.7 bln green bond approved by voters.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in New York State approved a $1.75 billion New York Clean Water, Clean Air Bond Act on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bond act, which was embraced by liberals and conservatives, Democrats and Republicans, would fund a variety of environmental projects throughout the state.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
